<p class="wp-block-paragraph">MailMaven (an occasional sponsor around here) <a href="https://mailmaven.app/">continues to evolve since their big launch last year</a>. Version 1.2 brings in automation with a full AppleScript dictionary for finding, examining, manipulating, and composing messages. If you&#8217;re a robot builder, you can <a href="https://github.com/Smallcubed/MailMavenMCP">tie that to the MCP</a>, and you&#8217;re really cooking.</p>

<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you&#8217;re not familiar with MailMaven, <a href="https://www.macsparky.com/blog/2025/11/mailmaven-a-new-mail-app-from-a-longtime-mail-plugin-developer/">I covered the backstory when they launched last November</a>: same folks who made the MailTags plugin for Apple Mail, forced into building their own app once Apple tightened the screws on plugins.</p><p>The post <a href="https://www.macsparky.com/blog/2026/08/mailmaven-adds-applescript-and-ai/">MailMaven Adds AppleScript and AI</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.macsparky.com">MacSparky</a>.</p>
